course: dictionary
lesson: 11111
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Whisk can be a thing or an action. A whisk is a kitchen tool made of curved wires. To whisk is to beat food fast, or to take someone away very quickly.
explain: The words around a word give you clues. «Cakes rise with baking powder or whisked eggs instead.» Cakes need something to make them rise, and whisked eggs do that job, so whisked must mean beaten fast to trap air.
explain: Look at the other words in the sentence to choose the right meaning. «Whisking cream traps air bubbles, held by fat droplets; whisking too long turns it lumpy and then into butter.» The cream, the bubbles and the lumps tell you that whisking is a cooking action.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it into the sentence in place of the word. If beat food fast with a whisk still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A whisk can be a noun: a kitchen tool made of curved wires.
fact: To whisk means to beat food fast, which adds air.
fact: To whisk someone or something away means to take them somewhere very quickly.
fact: «Whisk it gently instead» turns cream into whipped cream, because the fat holds air bubbles.
fact: Whisking too long turns cream lumpy, and then into butter.
exercise: «Cakes rise with baking powder or whisked eggs instead.» What does whisked mean here? | Left to cool | Taken away very quickly | Rubbed off, like a fly | *Beaten fast to trap air
exercise: Ben says a whisk must be a fast car, because it whisks. What is a whisk? | A fast car | *A kitchen tool made of curved wires | A type of cake | A jar for shaking cream
exercise: In «Whisk it gently instead», what kind of word is whisk? | A place | A thing you can wear | A colour | *A doing word, an action
test: What does whisking too long do to cream? | It makes it sweet and cold | *It turns it lumpy and then into butter | It makes it warm to touch | It turns it blue
test: A cow whisks its tail. What does whisk mean? | To sleep in the sun | To sing loudly | *To swish quickly to brush off flies | To bake a cake
exam: Lila says a car that whisks someone away is a kitchen tool. Is she right? | No, whisk only means to sing | Yes, it means to beat food fast | Yes, a car is a kitchen tool | *No, to whisk someone away means to take them somewhere very quickly
